Excluded from the Python distribution. The source stays, the wasm does not ship.

gpustack-lb in `mode: context` is a drop-in replacement for this plugin: on a
route with no `candidates` it degrades to exactly this behaviour, and it keeps
the `gpustack-model-mapper` CR name so an existing deployment upgrades in place.
Shipping both would put 6.0 MB of wasm (1.7 MB deflated) in every wheel for a
plugin nothing new should be pointed at.

The code is kept, and `make -C extensions test-all` keeps testing it, because
gpustack-lb's legacy path is meant to follow it verbatim -- it is the reference
for what "degrades to model-mapper" means, and a reference that no longer
compiles is worthless.

Effect of this file:

    make -C extensions build-all    skips this directory
    scripts/verify_whl.py           does not expect it in the wheel
    make -C extensions test-all     still runs its tests
    make -C extensions list         shows it, tagged [not packaged]

To build it anyway, name it explicitly -- that path ignores this marker:

    make -C extensions build PLUGIN_NAME=gpustack-model-mapper

To start shipping it again, delete this file. Nothing else references it by
name.
